    <title>Past Medical History</title>
    <text><paragraph>Historical biography with true dates. These events are not part of the synthetic care timeline.</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Historical date</th><th>History</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>about 1798</td><td>Hearing gradually weaker since about 1798, beginning in the left ear, with constant ringing and buzzing in both ears; high notes and soft speech hard to hear, and loud sounds unbearable</td><td>D (CLM-0004, CLM-0006)</td></tr><tr><td>until autumn 1800</td><td>Long-standing stomach complaint, which one physician held to be the cause of the hearing loss; treated with tonics, oil of almonds in the ears, and tepid baths, without benefit to his hearing</td><td>D (CLM-0004)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

