<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Professional pianist and composer; performs, teaches, and lives on commissions and a patron&apos;s yearly stipend; moved to this city from his home town about nine years ago [S]</item><item>Lives alone; has avoided parties and gatherings for about two years because he cannot follow conversation and does not want people to know he cannot hear [S]</item><item>Communication: German is his first language and he speaks fluent English; understands best face to face, one person at a time, in good light, and wants important details written down [S]</item><item>Alcohol: wine with dinner three or four evenings a week, two glasses at most (AUDIT-C 3); no tobacco or other drugs [S]</item><item>Noise exposure: hours of daily practice and rehearsal with orchestras; no hearing protection; no firearms or industrial noise; no known lead exposure at work or at home [S]</item><item>Wants his hearing loss kept private from employers and colleagues for now [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

