    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1801-04-13; see the Vital Signs section. Mental status: Alert, intense, and articulate; leans in and watches faces to follow speech; irritable when asked to repeat himself; Mood low and frustrated, with fear for his career; PHQ-9 score 12 with item 9 scored 0; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. The physical examination is limited to the findings relevant to this synthetic episode. [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Structured safety assessment: current ideation absent, intent absent, plan absent, access to means reviewed: yes. Outpatient care. No current thoughts of suicide or self-harm; no firearms at home. Isolation and fear for his career are risk factors, so safety will be reviewed at every visit. A written safety plan was made with him and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline was given, including its text and chat options, which he can use without hearing a voice on the phone. [S]</paragraph></text>

