    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Progressive hearing loss in both ears over about three years, worse on the left, with poor understanding of soft speech; type and cause not yet established at intake; audiology and otolaryngology evaluation requested: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Persistent, bothersome tinnitus in both ears for about three years, constant ringing and buzzing day and night, with intolerance of loud sound; synthetic modern episode linked to his documented tinnitus: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Adjustment disorder with depressed mood in response to progressive hearing loss, with withdrawal from social gatherings; synthetic modern episode linked to his documented despair and isolation: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Otolaryngology consultation with a same-day comprehensive audiologic evaluation: pure-tone air and bone conduction, speech audiometry with word recognition, tympanometry, and acoustic reflexes. Guideline: Clinical Practice Guideline: Tinnitus (Tunkel DE, et al. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2014;151(2 Suppl):S1-S40) (2014); Clinical Practice Guideline: Age-Related Hearing Loss (Tsai Do BS, et al. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2024;170 Suppl 2:S1-S54) (2024) [S]</item><item>Tests for treatable causes at intake: blood count, thyroid function, HbA1c, and treponemal antibody; no head imaging for the tinnitus alone. Guideline: Clinical Practice Guideline: Tinnitus (Tunkel DE, et al. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2014;151(2 Suppl):S1-S40) (2014); Clinical Practice Guideline: Sudden Hearing Loss (Update) (Chandrasekhar SS, et al. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2019;161(1_suppl):S1-S45) (2019) [S]</item><item>Tinnitus education, sound enrichment at night, and cognitive behavioral therapy with a psychologist for tinnitus distress and adjustment; no medication or supplements for tinnitus. Guideline: Clinical Practice Guideline: Tinnitus (Tunkel DE, et al. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg 2014;151(2 Suppl):S1-S40) (2014); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Depression monitoring with the PHQ-9 at each visit, a structured safety assessment with a written safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline (text and chat), and safety review at every visit. Guideline: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Communication access on his terms: his communication preferences on the chart, written summaries, captioning and speech-to-text, workplace accommodation when he chooses to ask, hearing loss peer support, and an introduction to the Deaf community and American Sign Language if he wishes. Guideline: ADA Requirements: Effective Communication (2026); Health Care and Mental Health Services: questions and answers for health care providers (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to otolaryngology, Ines Albrecht, MD, ordered 1801-04-13 [S]</item></list></text>

